  <title id="bdl05lowprecisionsgld-title">Histograms of low-precision SGLD samples on a standard Gaussian for two stepsizes</title>
  <desc id="bdl05lowprecisionsgld-desc">Six panels in two rows. Each panel shows a histogram of samples against the standard Gaussian density, drawn as a line. Top row, stepsize 0.001: naive SGLD with low-precision gradient accumulators gives a histogram that is too wide, with a peak of about 0.27 instead of 0.40, while the variance-corrected version and SGLD with full-precision gradient accumulators match the Gaussian. Bottom row, stepsize 0.0001: the naive histogram is wider still, spreading from about minus 7 to 7 with a peak of about 0.15, while the other two still match the Gaussian.</desc>
